  "subject": "A Pingtung roadside tyre-repair man finds a gold ring wedged in the tread of a scooter tyre and holds it up at the red light for every passing rider, until a delivery woman who lost it a week ago stops; she says she had already bought a new one but still wants this one.",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien Saharan desert blues, hypnotic Tuareg-style guitar groove. Electric guitar playing a looping pentatonic riff with dry, slightly gritty tone and hammer-ons; second guitar holding a steady droning bass figure; calabash and hand-drum percussion in a rolling shuffle; tindé-style skin drum on the offbeats; a small group answering the lead line in call-and-response. Dry live desert-band room sound, warm tape grit, no polish. Male baritone, warm and plain, clearly sung melody, one lead voice with a few answering voices. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 104 BPM, D minor. Wry, tender, roadside-patient. No rap, no trap hi-hats, no autotune, no synth pads, no EDM drop, no brass section.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n補胎仔店 佇路邊\n外胎剝落來 攤佇遐\n胎紋縫內 夾一箍物\n金金仔 是一个戒指\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n無名無姓 內面無字\n我共伊款佇 螺絲箱\n\n[Chorus]\n是啥人的戒指 失落去\n一路騎 一路揣\n我徛佇路邊 舉懸懸\n一台一台 看你欲停無\n\n[Verse]\n紅燈仔前 偌濟台機車\n我共戒指 舉予人看\n有人搖頭 有人笑\n有人催油 騎去矣\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n黃昏彼个 送貨的查某\n車停落來 手指摸一下\n\n[Chorus]\n是我的 失落的\n一禮拜 一路揣\n你徛佇路邊 舉懸懸\n這遍我總算 停落來\n\n[Verse]\n伊講 手指頭 瘦去\n袂牢 才會落佇路\n新的 早就買好矣\n舊的 我猶原欲愛\n\n[Bridge]\n沙塵 吹過 補胎店\n一圈一圈 輪攏袂停\n\n[Chorus]\n我替你 戴轉去彼隻手\n一路騎 免閣揣\n我徛佇路邊 看你\n騎去 前面彼个紅燈\n\n[Outro]\n胎補好矣 氣打飽矣\n戒指轉去 伊的手",
